## Claim reserves displayed in wrong currency; formatter updated to use claim record currency.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-700002)
**Module:** ClaimCenter | **Category:** UIRenderingBug | **Severity:** SEV3-Medium
**Resolution Type:** CodeFix
**Date:** 2025-11-30
**Guidewire Version:** Jasper

### Summary / Symptom
Claim reserve amounts on the adjuster dashboard are displaying in the wrong currency for international claims. USD amounts are being displayed as GBP for claims filed in the UK region. The correct currency is stored in the database but the display layer is showing the wrong symbol. Adjusters can see the correct value by running a manual report.

### Resolution
The adjuster dashboard was showing claim reserve amounts in GBP for UK claims, even when the actual values were stored in USD. This was caused by a hardcoded currency formatter that defaulted to GBP based on office code, rather than reading the correct currency from the claim record. The issue was resolved by updating the formatter to use the currency code stored in each claim. No underlying data was incorrect; only the display label was affected.


