## Payment plan reassignment failed for migrated policies due to missing template ID mapping; data backfilled.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-700003)
**Module:** BillingCenter | **Category:** DataCorruption | **Severity:** SEV2-High
**Resolution Type:** DataRemediation
**Date:** 2025-11-30

### Summary / Symptom
Payment plan reassignment is failing for policies that were migrated from the legacy billing system. When an agent tries to change the payment plan on a migrated policy, BillingCenter throws a foreign key constraint violation. Agents can manually recreate the policy in BillingCenter as a workaround but it takes 30 minutes per policy.

### Resolution
The root cause was that migrated policies from the legacy billing system lacked the required payment_plan_template_id, as the migration script did not map legacy plan codes to the new BillingCenter template IDs. This resulted in foreign key constraint violations when agents attempted to reassign payment plans. The issue was resolved by updating the migration reference table with the correct template ID mappings and running a backfill to update all affected policies. Agents no longer need to manually recreate policies, as the data is now consistent.


