## Inbound mobile FNOLs dropped due to expired SSL certificate; records manually recreated after renewal.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-700004)
**Module:** IntegrationGateway | **Category:** IntegrationFailure | **Severity:** SEV1-Critical
**Resolution Type:** DataRemediation
**Date:** 2025-12-01
**Guidewire Version:** Innsbruck

### Summary / Symptom
All inbound FNOL notifications from the mobile app are being dropped. Claims are not being created in ClaimCenter from mobile submissions. The mobile app shows a success confirmation to customers but no claim appears in the system. Approximately 90 mobile FNOLs have been silently lost since yesterday evening.

### Resolution
The root cause was an expired SSL certificate on the inbound FNOL API endpoint, which caused the API gateway to silently drop all mobile FNOL submissions despite the mobile app showing a success confirmation. The issue was resolved by renewing the SSL certificate and restarting the API gateway. Additionally, the 90 lost FNOL records were manually recreated using logs from the mobile app submissions to restore the missing claims.


